# No Comments

Do not add comments to code you write or edit.

- No explanatory comments, section headers, or narrating what the next line does
- No JSDoc/TSDoc on obvious functions, props, or types
- Prefer clear names and structure over comments
- Leave existing comments alone unless asked to change or remove them
- Only add a comment when the user explicitly asks for one, or when a non-obvious constraint/workaround cannot be expressed in code

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
// Format the title for Etsy
const title = formatListingTitle(input);

// ✅ GOOD
const title = formatListingTitle(input);
```
